"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"231ec3cc92dd94ab96a5a4833b91f54340d30e9815060dd668d43c3cd0b5e530","event_uuid":"9766b86b-e648-4a96-b20d-15092ff7b784","position":{"commit_sha":"2eabb51f324fdf1127d8346db77dc2931696be80","position":"1795183833469453001-9766b86b-e648-4a96-b20d-15092ff7b784"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"dafa84408e31537dad98ab4eb5dedf5601e65c0bea1cefea7ec2081e23aca008","event_uuid":"fb32a4f2-9568-4cc6-8361-b3300898cdc5","position":{"commit_sha":"a578b526229388a4a5359955476fc230f696a436","position":"1795187054612187209-fb32a4f2-9568-4cc6-8361-b3300898cdc5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Evidence (2026-11-20 PST). Inside the agent sandbox on origin/main: probe available=True, os.sysconf('SC_SEM_NSEMS_MAX') -> PermissionError [Errno 1], ProcessPoolExecutor(1) -> same error; the test fails 'PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted' (1 failed in 119.81 s). With commit 2b5e23a32c0 (Gerrit 3480; plain spawn-context Processes + one-way Pipes, no per-worker bound): inside the sandbox 1 passed in 208.76 s. The plan's first draft (widen the shared probe) was blocked in review because 3 other marked tests need only SemLock and would have been skipped needlessly; the revised plan passed. Local make verify not run for this change: all 3 shared verify slots were held by this session's other changes, and those runs show about 20 unrelated 300 s pytest-timeout expiries each at load 30-45 (see rubbery-adamantine-panda).","timestamp":1795183833469453001}],"created_at":1795179068115601001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b214e678-768a-4201-8abe-e96f544e77b1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c0ed-53e2-aa14-48f8"},{"link_uuid":"d38399b0-37ea-4f04-8212-bbb1d3a78143","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9b8a-60c3-2194-418c"},{"link_uuid":"fb32a4f2-9568-4cc6-8361-b3300898cdc5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"458c-7125-425d-4488"}],"description":"## Observation\nA sandboxed local `make verify` (worktree almondy-drop-acl-step, Nov 19 18:23 to Nov 20 01:14 PST, tree origin/main 717c50f8b33 plus a workflow-only change) failed `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_two_processes_publish_at_most_one_equivalent_same_ticket_bundle` at `ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=2)` (test line 399) with `PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted`, raised from CPython 3.12 `concurrent/futures/process.py:613`. That line is `os.sysconf(\"SC_SEM_NSEMS_MAX\")` in `_check_system_limits`, which catches only AttributeError and ValueError. The same change passed CI Verified (Gerrit 3475, run 44732620097).\n\nThe test carries `@pytest.mark.requires_posix_named_semaphore`, whose conftest hook skips it (counted) when `tests/_sandbox_capabilities.posix_named_semaphore_probe()` reports unavailable. That probe only constructs a `_multiprocessing.SemLock`.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-20 on this host, same interpreter: inside the Claude Code sandbox the probe returns `available=True`, `os.sysconf(\"SC_SEM_NSEMS_MAX\")` raises `PermissionError [Errno 1]`, and `ProcessPoolExecutor(1)` raises the same error. Outside the sandbox sysconf returns 87381 and the pool runs. So the failure is deterministic under the sandbox and is not load-related.\n\n## Root cause\nThe probe checks a different capability from the one the marked tests need: the sandbox allows SemLock creation but denies the sysconf query that ProcessPoolExecutor makes first. The marker therefore does not skip a test the host cannot run.\n\n## Approach\nFix the test, not the probe. The probe (`tests/_sandbox_capabilities.posix_named_semaphore_probe`) is shared by 4 marked tests; 3 of them need only `SemLock`, which the sandbox allows, so widening the probe would skip tests that run correctly there. Only this test goes through `ProcessPoolExecutor`, whose sysconf query the sandbox denies.\n\nIn `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py`, replace the `ProcessPoolExecutor` with 2 plain `multiprocessing` spawn-context `Process`es. Each runs `_commit_worker`, which sends `(\"ok\", atomic_close)` or `(\"error\", repr)` back over a one-way `Pipe`; the parent receives both outcomes and joins the workers. The same rewrite drops the `future.result(timeout=60)` per-worker wall-clock bound filed as sweltering-difficult-drongo: the suite's 300 s per-test budget bounds a hang. The race the test checks (2 processes publish the same bundle; exactly one is non-idempotent) is unchanged. The `requires_posix_named_semaphore` marker stays, since `Pipe`/`Process` still need it on hosts without POSIX semaphores. No probe, marker, config key, environment variable, or flag changes.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py`\n\n## Testing\n- Inside the agent sandbox: before, the test fails with `PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted` (measured 2026-11-20, 1 failed in 119.81 s); after, it runs and passes (measured: 1 passed in 208.76 s, load average ~30).\n- Outside the sandbox: the test passes with the change.\n- The module `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py` passes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Inside the agent sandbox the atomic-close test runs and passes instead of failing on the sysconf query (before/after runs recorded here); outside the sandbox it still passes.\n- [ ] The test no longer uses ProcessPoolExecutor or a per-worker wall-clock bound.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the change.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py","reason":"race the two workers with plain processes and no per-worker wall bound"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","458c-7125-425d-4488"],["relates_to","9b8a-60c3-2194-418c"],["relates_to","c0ed-53e2-aa14-48f8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"614f2f26-6a80-48c6-8281-8414eee9f9c9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fa59-9a21-097b-49be","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Semaphore capability probe passes in the agent sandbox, but ProcessPoolExecutor still fails on os.sysconf EPERM","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7ac2eef9-6da1-41f1-a51a-8afc9b0a2460","c90c01ab-26da-4620-ab7a-2e3a32dce972","3bac88ee-cc79-4fd4-ac86-04beae10ab24","b214e678-768a-4201-8abe-e96f544e77b1","d38399b0-37ea-4f04-8212-bbb1d3a78143","01050beb-feb1-41ac-bbd4-8acb16468464","6629d14f-5bfe-4e7c-bed0-1ef1484989c7","aee5da75-dc5f-49e7-b43e-3e8a74ede8f4","614f2f26-6a80-48c6-8281-8414eee9f9c9","515d3fac-be97-4358-b6e2-b9f6db080cc1","9766b86b-e648-4a96-b20d-15092ff7b784","fb32a4f2-9568-4cc6-8361-b3300898cdc5"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795187054612187210,"uuid":"db94ab3d-8be3-4f64-bfc0-7f46a365adda"}